            {
                "entry_id": "e03d278e-a901-38a4-a636-25ecbbec70bd",
                "word": "dojo",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "875821b1-bb09-3ae0-a7f8-9e8b5870b056",
                        "entry_id": "e03d278e-a901-38a4-a636-25ecbbec70bd",
                        "glosses": [
                            "The dojo loach, Japanese weather loach, or pond loach (Misgurnus anguillicaudatus), a freshwater fish native to East Asia."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "87d7ac68-2975-4665-9bd8-a3181ed62d5f",
                                "sense_id": "875821b1-bb09-3ae0-a7f8-9e8b5870b056",
                                "text": "The head of the dojô is small, the mouth is surrounded by six or eight barbules as is the case with several species of fish which inhabit muddy streams. [...] A microscopic examination showed them [the barbules] to be rich in muscular fibres for movement, and through the centre run a thick bundle of very delicate nerve fibres which spread out on the surface of each barbule's tip. These, I suppose from the manner which the dojô dips its head down, assist in the search for food, [...]"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "88e6acec-23ae-4511-bc25-f9a73c783b8b",
                                "sense_id": "875821b1-bb09-3ae0-a7f8-9e8b5870b056",
                                "text": "[A] comparative test on susceptibility to E1-43, 064 between the goldfish and ‘Dojo’ fish was made by dipping method. The result has shown that the ‘Dojo’ fish is 5.32 times as susceptible as the goldfish to E1-43, 064."
                            },
                            {
